WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.890
So the job of the writer
is not to supply the ideas,

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.945
it is to be patient
enough to find the ideas.

00:00:07.945 --> 00:00:10.630
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.200
David and Goliath is a
concept we all know--

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.219
an arrogant big dude who thinks
he's fighting a sword fight,

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:18.720
and David changed the rules.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.810
But then, I stumbled
across this paper

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.630
that had been written by an
Israeli endocrinologist, who

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.020
had suggested Goliath
has this really

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.210
rare medical
condition which causes

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.090
you to lose your eyesight.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.100
Why do giants lose?

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.270
Because they can't see.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.430
They're so big and
strong and powerful,

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.560
they lose the ability
to kind of properly

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.720
appreciate the
world around them.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.850
It's not just a story about
David's courage and greatness.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:51.700
It's a story about
Goliath's blindness.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.030
You can find gold in
the smallest of details

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:56.395
if you're willing to be patient.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.540
We're going to talk about
suspense, structure, research,

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.390
humility, characters,
puzzles, and semi-colons.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:09.730
One of the mistakes
I think writers make

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:11.440
is they spend a lot
of time thinking

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.170
about how to start their stories
and not a lot of time thinking

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.030
about how to end them.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:19.660
Knowing my ending makes the
beginning super easy, right?

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:22.060
It's totally clear what I
have to do and totally clear

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.650
what I shouldn't do.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.980
Your first goal is to
be pure and simple,

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.430
to write at an
eighth grade level,

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:30.660
but with ideas that are
super sophisticated.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:34.480
All good nonfiction writing
is about going out and finding

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.240
someone else and
inhabiting their world

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.270
and representing it to readers.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.910
It is giving us a window into
other people's hearts and souls

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.330
and minds.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.980
I'm Malcolm Gladwell, and
this is my master class.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.030
[MUSIC PLAYING]

